@page
@model PrivacyModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy";
}

<div class="container policy-shell py-5">
    <article class="policy-card">
        <span class="section-kicker">YOUR DATA, YOUR CHOICE</span>
        <h1>Privacy at Finance Freedom</h1>
        <p class="policy-updated">Plain-language privacy notice · Updated 9 October 2026</p>

        <div class="policy-callout">
            <strong>Your financial entries are private to your account.</strong>
            <span>Finance Freedom uses them to provide your personal budget and reports. They are not used to choose advertising.</span>
        </div>

        <h2>Information this app uses</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Account details:</strong> your email address and a securely hashed password for sign-in.</li>
            <li><strong>Finance entries:</strong> transaction dates, descriptions, categories, types, amounts, and budgets you choose to enter.</li>
            <li><strong>Plan details:</strong> the current version is free and ad-supported. The app stores your plan status to manage account features.</li>
            <li><strong>Basic technical data:</strong> the app uses an authentication cookie to keep you signed in and security features to protect account forms.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>How information is used</h2>
        <p>Your account and finance entries are used to show your dashboard, calculate weekly and monthly summaries, save budgets, and provide features you request. Finance Freedom only serves ads after consent and required publisher setup.</p>
        <p>Bank linking and investment features are currently unavailable in Finance Freedom. The app does not connect a bank or retrieve investment data. If you used an earlier bank-linking preview, any saved connection summaries are removed when you delete your account.</p>
        <p>The AdSense verification code is loaded in the site header. The app's manual ad placement is limited to public educational guides and stays disabled until the site operator has AdSense approval and configured Google's consent message or another certified consent management platform for the regions served. Google and its advertising partners may receive device and usage information when the code loads; if ads are enabled, they may also use cookies or similar technologies to provide, measure, and personalise advertising according to your choices and applicable settings. You can review or change those choices in the consent message. The operator should keep Auto ads disabled or exclude authenticated finance pages so ads do not appear beside private transaction and savings figures.</p>

        <h2>Payments</h2>
        <p>Paid subscriptions are not part of the current ad-supported launch. Finance Freedom does not receive or store your payment card number. If paid features are introduced later, this notice will be updated before they are offered.</p>

        <h2>Storage and security</h2>
        <p>When run locally, the app uses separate SQLite files for account and finance data. The included public-hosting configuration uses a managed PostgreSQL database with separate account and finance schemas. Finance records are queried using the signed-in account ID. Authentication cookies use ASP.NET Identity and data-protection keys are persisted in the database so sessions survive service restarts.</p>
        <p>Hosting, backups, and database access are managed by the site operator. No online service can promise absolute security. The operator should publish its legal identity, contact details, hosting region, retention schedule, and data request process before accepting public registrations.</p>

        <h2>Your choices</h2>
        <p>You can review your account in Account settings and permanently delete your Finance Freedom profile, transactions, any saved bank connection summaries, and budgets there. If an older account has a separate payment subscription, its records and cancellation are subject to that payment provider's terms.</p>
        <p>For a data access or privacy request, email <a href="mailto:Zection6@gmail.com">Zection6@gmail.com</a>.</p>

        <h2>Contact and data requests</h2>
        <p>Before opening public registration, the site operator must replace this launch notice with its legal name, contact address, hosting location, retention periods, and applicable jurisdiction-specific rights. Until those details are published, do not enter real financial information.</p>
        <a class="btn btn-outline-primary mt-3" asp-page="/Account/Manage">Go to account settings</a>
        <a class="btn btn-outline-primary mt-3" asp-page="/Contact">Contact us</a>
    </article>
</div>
